# Qualified Personal Residence Trust (QPRT)

An irrevocable trust that transfers a residence to trust while the settlor retains the right to live in the property for a term, then transfers it to beneficiaries at discounted value.

## Structure

- Home transferred to trust
- Settlor retains right to live in property
- Fixed term (usually 10-15 years)
- Remainder interest passes to beneficiaries at term end
- Must meet IRS requirements for qualified transfer

## Tax Benefits

- Gift tax discount from present value of retained interest
- Home removed from taxable estate at term end
- Future appreciation passes to beneficiaries tax-free
- Probate avoidance for residence
- Asset protection after transfer

## Planning Considerations

- Term selection balances retained interest vs. tax benefit
- Life expectancy considerations for term length
- IRS 7520 rate impact
- Proper valuation of residence
- Proper transfer of residence title

